", "links": [2], "label": "positive", "type": "CONDITIONING", "localized_name": "positive"}, {"name": "LATENT", "links": [7], "label": "LATENT", "type": "LATENT", "localized_name": "Latent"}], "size": [420.1185302734375, 568.0217895507812], "pos": [2078.454833984375, 723.6602783203125], "widgets_values": ["subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the swordswoman in <Picture 1>, a young woman with long dark hair, a small crown-like updo secured by hairpins, soft pink lips, wearing a flowing layered white silk hanfu with wide trailing sleeves, a white wrapped waist sash, and silver-buckled belt; she wields a long single-handed jian with a silver guard and pale grip.\n<Subject 2> is the swordswoman in <Picture 2>, a young woman with long dark hair half-pinned by a small floral pin, soft pink lips, wearing a layered pale-mint hanfu with sheer off-the-shoulder draped sleeves, a wide teal waist sash tied in a bow, and hanging jade tassels; she wields a long single-handed jian with a pale grip and silver guard.\n<Subject 3> is the raised circular dueling platform beneath the duelists, a polished pale-wood floor ringed by a low carved balustrade and tall crimson lanterns, with drifting pink cherry blossom petals filling the air around the ring and a soft ring of incense smoke drifting at floor level.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] The target video is a 6-second cinematic wuxia duel on <Subject 3>. <Subject 1> and <Subject 2> face off and engage in a rapid, fluid exchange of thrusts, parries, and acrobatic strikes, with cherry petals swirling around every clash, ending frozen in a final crossed-blade lock at the center of the ring.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - the white silk hanfu, wide trailing sleeves, wrapped waist sash, updo with hairpins, and silver-guard jian are retained throughout.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - the pale-mint hanfu, off-the-shoulder sheer sleeves, teal bow sash, jade tassels, floral hairpin, and pale-grip jian are retained throughout.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - the circular wood dueling platform, low carved balustrade, crimson lanterns, and drifting cherry petals are retained across all shots.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses a cinematic live-action wuxia style with high-contrast daylight, soft volumetric backlight through the cherry trees, and a slight slow-motion effect reserved for the moment of blade contact.\n[Shot 1] A medium-wide shot at ring level establishes <Subject 3>: a circular pale-wood dueling platform ringed by a low carved balustrade, tall crimson lanterns glowing at the four compass points, cherry blossom petals drifting in slow spirals through cold blue-white daylight. <Subject 1> stands on the left side of the ring in a low ready stance, her white silk sleeves hanging loose, the silver-guard jian held at her right hip, blade angled down. <Subject 2> mirrors her on the right side of the ring, pale-mint sleeves flowing, jian held at her left hip in a parallel guard, their eyes locked across the polished floor. Without a beat, both explode forward at the same instant: <Subject 1> launches a diagonal downward slash from upper right, <Subject 2> answers with an upward parry, the two blades collide center-frame in a bright shower of sparks and burst of torn cherry petals. The camera tracks the engagement from a low arc, swinging around the clashing pair as they pivot through the first bind, both already repositioning for the next strike.\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.000, the shot cuts to a rapid sequence: a tight side close-up of <Subject 1>'s blade snapping forward in a straight thrust toward <Subject 2>'s shoulder, <Subject 2> twisting her torso to let the tip graze past her cheek as she counters with a horizontal cut at <Subject 1>'s midsection. The camera whips right at fast speed as <Subject 1> drops into a deep backbend, the green blade passing a hair's breadth over her stomach, and fires back an upward rising slash that <Subject 2> blocks at the last instant with a crossed-blade parry overhead. They spring apart, then close again instantly: a low-angle shot from the platform floor shows them both leaping into the air simultaneously, jians swinging in a tight overhead scissor strike, the two blades locking and spinning them in a single aerial pirouette before they break apart and land back-to-back on the platform, capes and sleeves fanning outward, cherry petals swirling around them in a slow vortex.\n[Shot 3] At 00:04.500, the shot cuts to a wide shot from beyond the balustrade. <Subject 1> pivots first, launching a fast three-cut combo: thrust, horizontal slash, rising cut, each one seamlessly flowing into the next. <Subject 2> gives ground two steps, deflects the first thrust with a small circular parry, redirects the second slash past her hip, and turns the third strike aside with a rising block that she immediately converts into a counterthrust aimed at <Subject 1>'s throat. <Subject 1> drops her chin and deflects the counterthrust with a flat palm against the flat of <Subject 2>'s blade, then in a single explosive motion drives her own jian forward into a final straight thrust aimed at <Subject 2>'s chest. The camera pushes in at fast speed as <Subject 2> meets the thrust with her own blade extended; the two jians meet point-to-guard in the exact center of the frame, lock together, and stop dead, both women frozen in a hard forward stance, blades crossed and trembling, sleeves and hair still settling around them, cherry petals drifting past in slow motion as the ring falls silent.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nThe duel sits inside a hushed cherry grove with a faint wind moving through the trees, a single distant temple bell, and the soft susurration of drifting petals. The two blades produce sharp, ringing metallic clashes on every contact, layered with the scuff of silk and the rhythmic double-thud of footwork on polished wood. The aerial pirouette adds a brief whip of fabric and a hard landing impact, and the final crossed-blade lock ends with a long, sustained metallic ring that decays slowly into silence.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA driving Chinese-style drum pattern at a fast tempo, anchored by a low guzheng ostinato and a single sustained xiao note that cuts in across the first bind, builds through the three-cut combo, and resolves on a single reverberating drum hit at the final blade lock, fading into the long metallic tail of the crossed swords.\n", 1344, 768, 124, "match"], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 15, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"name": "vae", "link": 16, "label": "vae", "type": "VAE", "localized_name": "vae"}, {"name": "audio_vae", "link": 17, "label": "audio_vae", "type": "VAE", "localized_name": "audio_vae"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_images.ref_image_0", "link": 18, "label": "ref_images.ref_image_0", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image_0"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_videos.ref_video_0", "label": "ref_videos.ref_video_0", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_video_0"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_video_audios.ref_video_audio_0", "label": "ref_video_audios.ref_video_audio_0", "type": "AUDIO", "localized_name": "ref_video_audio_0"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_audios.ref_audio_0", "label": "ref_audios.ref_audio_0", "type": "AUDIO", "localized_name": "ref_audio_0"}, {"widget": {"name": "prompt"}, "name": "prompt", "label": "prompt", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "prompt"}, {"widget": {"name": "width"}, "name": "width", "link": 24, "label": "width", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "width"}, {"widget": {"name": "height"}, "name": "height", "link": 25, "label": "height", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "height"}, {"widget": {"name": "length"}, "name": "length", "link": 26, "label": "length", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "length"}, {"widget": {"name": "ref_image_size"}, "name": "ref_i